ent\n- Emitted events validate against the published common audit event schema\n- Delivery to the cluster audit sink is at-least-once: a test that restarts the\n  emitting component while inference traffic is flowing shows no audit event loss\n- Setting the per-project audit configuration to disabled suppresses event\n  emission for that project; enabled resumes emission\n- The build pipeline is green on the changes\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0) — every inference request through a KServe endpoint emits an audit\n  event capturing caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and response status\n  (not payloads)\n- HLR-2 (P0) — audit events are delivered to the cluster audit sink with\n  at-least-once semantics and are not lost on component restart\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33685,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba496536d9bd8d7a","agent_id":"aa5df267111b6dd19","session_id":"2349ced6-e096-4fba-9cc4-d111ca7d4c3d","uuid":"7c7e7c55-4c93-460f-ac2a-88fd8d089d30","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:08:26.233Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9010"}
