\t  existing Dashboard permission patterns\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- An administrator can enable and disable inference auditing for a specific\n56\t  project from the Dashboard\n57\t- The setting takes effect on the serving side: audit events are emitted for\n58\t  the project when enabled and suppressed when disabled\n59\t- The Dashboard displays the current per-project auditing state accurately\n60\t- The control is not exposed to users without administrator-level project\n61\t  access, consistent with existing Dashboard permission behavior\n62\t- The build pipeline is green on the changes\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-3 (P1) — administrators can enable/disable inference auditing per project\n67\t  from the Dashboard\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b64ac9384f034fea","agent_id":"a4ab00141ce8272de","session_id":"2349ced6-e096-4fba-9cc4-d111ca7d4c3d","uuid":"0e26b4e4-8aad-4362-96d8-ac5620847705","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:10:28.523Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b23bd578817ae37b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9010 decomposition"}
