{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-827f56caf8cad706","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9010-E002\n3\ttitle: Emit inference audit events from KServe with reliable delivery to the cluster\n4\t  audit sink\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9010\n6\tcomponent: KServe\n7\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9010-E001\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 5\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Emit inference audit events from KServe with reliable delivery to the cluster audit sink\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic implements the core compliance capability: every inference request\n36\tthrough a KServe endpoint emits a structured audit event — capturing caller\n37\tidentity, model/version, timestamp, and response status (never payloads) — and\n38\tthe event is delivered to the cluster audit sink with at-least-once semantics\n39\tthat survive component restarts. Events conform to the published common audit\n40\tevent schema so they are interpretable by auditors and compatible with future\n41\tcomponents' events.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Emit an audit event on the KServe inference request path for every inference\n46\t  request, capturing caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and response\n47\t  status; no request or response payload content is captured\n48\t- Conform all emitted events to the published common audit event schema\n49\t- Deliver events to the cluster audit sink (the standard cluster logging\n50\t  forwarder) with at-least-once semantics\n51\t- Buffer and retry delivery so events are not lost when the emitting component\n52\t  restarts\n53\t- Provide a per-project audit enablement configuration that the serving stack\n54\t  honors (auditing on/off per project) — this is the surface the Dashboard\n55\t  administration capability writes; the exact mechanism (CR field vs. config\n56\t  resource) is an implementation decision for the serving team\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Every inference request through a KServe endpoint produces exactly the\n61\t  required audit event fields (caller identity, model/version, timestamp,\n62\t  response status) and no payload content\n63\t- Emitted events validate against the published common audit event schema\n64\t- Delivery to the cluster audit sink is at-least-once: a test that restarts the\n65\t  emitting component while inference traffic is flowing shows no audit event loss\n66\t- Setting the per-project audit configuration to disabled suppresses event\n67\t  emission for that project; enabled resumes emission\n68\t- The build pipeline is green on the changes\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-1 (P0) — every inference request through a KServe endpoint emits an audit\n73\t  event capturing caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and response status\n74\t  (not payloads)\n75\t- HLR-2 (P0) — audit events are delivered to the cluster audit sink with\n76\t  at-least-once semantics and are not lost on component restart\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81e22835b848ba2e","agent_id":"a3ae4796c76551536","session_id":"2349ced6-e096-4fba-9cc4-d111ca7d4c3d","uuid":"fffaf419-b261-4bca-9eec-7dded7d22051","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:15:16.966Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-827f56caf8cad706","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9010 decomposition"}
